Heh, I _thought_ *{bongnanba} seemed inordinately hard to pronounce. I appl=
ied this change and ran mukti's list through. The remaining non-parsing wor=
ds are:

klivlynd
smanyjinkytoldu'evir

artmozaiko
finprsinxnatfidai
finprsinxnatfinai
klaktno
mastla
mustlei
postmo
rartni
runtngasnrproni
sparknipofia
venzla
xipfne

bangrtlingana
banrtlingana
banrtlinganu
bongnanba
gudjrati
ingmeme


So just two that you weren't expecting, nice! I didn't check any words not =
in mukti's list, though.

As for fixing, I'd expect that many of these words weren't expecting a cons=
onantal syllable (*{klivlynd}, *{postmo}, *{artmozaiko}), so the fix might =
be to add a syllable: {artamozaiko} or {artnmozaiko}. I can't see how to ma=
ke "Cleveland" without adding a pause to get two cmevla {.kliv.lynd.}.

mu'o mi'e la durkavore =20


